Description: Use system libc++ for protoc-gen-js (avoid bundled libc++ locale dependency)
 protoc-gen-js requires locale.cpp symbols which cannot be compiled with
 bundled libc++ setup (namespace errors with __newlocale/__freelocale).
 .
 Missing symbols with bundled libc++: std::__Cr::locale::*, std::__Cr::num_put::id,
 std::__Cr::ctype::id, std::__Cr::codecvt::id, __cxa_guard_*, __cxa_pure_virtual
 .
 Solution: Use system libc++ for this build tool only. Since protoc-gen-js
 is a host build tool (not linked into CEF runtime), namespace differences
 between system std::__1 and bundled std::__Cr are acceptable.
 .
 Build 135: Proven locale.cpp compilation impossible
 Build 161: Failed with bundled libc++ (locale symbols missing)
 Build 162: Failed without explicit libc++ dep (same errors)
 Build 163: Use system libc++ (this patch)
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-13

--- a/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
@@ -20,6 +20,10 @@ if (current_toolchain == host_toolchain) {
     ]
     configs -= [ "//build/config/compiler:chromium_code" ]
     configs += [ "//build/config/compiler:no_chromium_code" ]
+
+    # Debian: Override -nostdlib++ and use system libc++ (provides locale symbols)
+    ldflags = [ "-stdlib=libc++" ]
+    libs = [ "c++", "c++abi" ]
   }
 }

+
